<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Newcrest Q1 net profit A$154 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Newcrest Q1 net profit A$154 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended Sept 30</p>
<p>	    (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit after abnormals   154.0 vs  6.1</p>
<p>NOTE: Gold miner Newcrest Mining Ltd said net profit before abnormal items was A$9.6 million for the first quarter.</p>
<p>It said it booked an abnormal profit of A$270 million on the closeout of a gold hedge position.  </p>
<p>    Sales				 89.8 vs 89.1</p>
<p>    Other income			 7.3 vs  0.2</p>
<p>    Abnormals (total)		225.6 vs nil</p>
<p>    Tax				   84.9 vs  5.0</p>
<p>    Depreciation			14.1 vs 14.4</p>
<p>NOTES: Newcrest said abnormals also included a A$47.6 million loss due to balance sheet adjustments and the profit on the sale of Ora Banda.  </p>
<p>It said group equity gold production was 134,238 ounces in the three months to September 30, compared with 151,094 ounces a year earlier. Cost of production was A$392 per ounce, compared with A$393 per ounce.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
